  ('052905e9-f404-5a9e-97d7-99d6e17ba349', '6c8eb00a-f68f-5306-9d35-ae99f729e52b', null, 'usr-slack-velen', 'CVS-4  :large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: raw_cu_v1.inventory_observations  _Have feedback on this insight?_  CU raw inventory collection coverage degraded after 2026-06-29 UTC  *UTC analysis:* 2026-06-15 ~ 2026-06-29 versus 2026-06-29 ~ 2026-07-13. *Base:* N=14 calendar days in each window.  CU raw inventory collection covered *12 of 14 days (85.7143%)* before 2026-06-29, versus *3 of 14 days (21.4286%)* afterward—a decline of *64.2857 percentage points (75.0000%)*. Raw observation rows fell from *15,753 to 6,048*, while distinct source objects fell from *15,752 to 3,837*. This is a *data-integrity/collection-coverage finding*, not evidence that curated event cadence stopped. [1] [2]  CU raw inventory collection coverage by UTC period  *Recommended actions*  - Data Collection / Crawler owner: inspect CU crawler run logs and the raw_cu_v1.inventory_observations ingestion path for 2026-06-29 ~ 2026-07-13 UTC; identify which expected collection dates and source-object retrievals are absent, plus the first failing run or configuration change. - Data Engineering: reconcile crawler output against raw_cu_v1.inventory_observations for the same UTC window, checking scheduler execution, write success, and source-object-key uniqueness; restore and monitor a daily coverage check with a 14-day denominator. - Analytics / Reporting owners: qualify inferred-sales reporting for dates on or after 2026-06-29 UTC as coverage-limited until the collection gap is explained and coverage is restored; validate the affected CU date range before using those outputs in decisions.', '2026-07-13T08:00:11.508Z', '2026-07-13T08:00:11.508Z', '[{"type": "header", "block_id": "zCVkv", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "CVS-4", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "context", "block_id": "coufk", "elements": [{"type": "mrkdwn", "text": ":large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: raw_cu_v