- CU: 실패 / latest=2026-07-17T07:14:22.870Z / detail=phase=failed / status=failure / recent_failures=317', '2026-07-17T07:23:19.367Z', '2026-07-17T07:23:19.367Z', '[{"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "yB8", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "[cu-crawl] 시스템 상태 실패 감지", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n- 기준 시각: 2026-07-17T07:23:19.035Z\n- 실패 컴포넌트: 2\n- D1: 장애 / latest=2026-07-17T07:23:10.136Z / detail=Cloudflare D1 storage API is not configured. Set CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_D1_DATABASE_ID, and CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN.\n- CU: 실패 / latest=2026-07-17T07:14:22.870Z / detail=phase=failed / status=failure / recent_failures=317"}]}]}]'),
  ('b0772c7d-6e89-57b7-a82c-6258dcf09954', '6c8eb00a-f68f-5306-9d35-ae99f729e52b', null, 'usr-slack-velen', 'CVS-8  :large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales, curated_inventory_v2.current_store_item_state  _Have feedback on this insight?_  Quarantine TOUSLESJOURS long-interval allocations from demand reporting  *Decision:* Treat the apparent TOUSLESJOURS movement as a reporting-quality risk—not genuine demand growth—and exclude long-interval allocations from current demand reporting until the observation cadence is validated.  *UTC analysis period:* previous window *2026-07-03 ~ 2026-07-09* versus current window *2026-07-10 ~ 2026-07-16*. *Base:* previous N=2,147,330 and current N=2,171,352 total inferred units.  - Long-interval allocations represented 2,166,889 of 2,171,352 inferred units (99.79%) in the current window, up from 75,794 of 2,147,330 (3.53%) previously. Total inferred units increased by only 24,022, while long-interval units increased by 2,091,095, so the apparent movement is dominated by allocation methodology rather than a comparable demand signal. [1] - The long-interval share exceeded 99.5% on every date from 2026-07-10 through 2026-07-16, after rising sharply between 2026-07-07 and 2026-07-09. [2] - The pattern is also present at the source-interval level: intervals longer than 24 hours rose to 83,850 of 85,508 unique intervals (98.06%) from 12,141 of 152,040 (7.99%). [3] - This is material beyond TOUSLESJOURS reporting: the affected 2,166,889 units were 64.11% of 3,379,827 inferred units across all covered providers in the current window. [4] - The increase was broad: the largest store contributed only 11.49% of the long-interval-unit increase. [5]  Daily share of TOUSLESJOURS inferred units allocated from long intervals  Observation gaps or crawler-cadence degradation are plausible hypotheses, but the operational cause is not proven. The current-state surface ends at *2026-07-14 21:58:41.734 UTC*, while the hourly surface extends to *2026-07-17 06:00:00 UTC*, reinforcing the need for run-level validation rather than a causal conclusion. [6] [7]  Recommended actions  1. Demand-reporting owner: In TOUSLESJOURS dashboards and downstream demand extracts, immediately quarantine rows where interval_quality_status = ''long_interval'' or interval_duration_seconds &gt; 86400; publish both included and excluded unit totals so stakeholders can verify the reporting impact. [1] 2. Crawler/data-engineering owner: Inspect run-level crawler logs and observation-completion metrics around 2026-07-07 ~ 2026-07-09 UTC, segmented by store, to identify missed or delayed observation runs before deciding whether to reprocess affected intervals. [2] [5] 3. Data-platform owner: Refresh current_store_item_state, then reconcile its latest TOUSLESJOURS observation timestamp against hourly_inferred_sales; restore current reporting only after the freshness gap and long-interval share return to an accepted threshold. [6] [7]', '2026-07-17T08:00:13.640Z', '2026-07-17T08:00:13.640Z', '[{"type": "header", "block_id": "iClZ0", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "CVS-8", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "context", "block_id": "3j/20", "elements": [{"type": "mrkdwn", "text": ":large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales, curated_inventory_v2.current_store_item_state", "verbatim": false}]}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "slack_feedback_open_block", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "_Have feedback on this insight?_", "verbatim": false}, "accessory": {"type": "button", "action_id": "slack_feedback_open", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Feedback", "emoji": true}, "accessibility_label": "Share feedback on this insight", "value": "{\"insightId\":\"01KXQDR92C2925J283Z2FTTPGR\",\"source\":\"slack_message_button\"}"}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "q4NOT", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Quarantine TOUSLESJOURS long-interval allocations from demand reporting", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "N49Ti", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*Decision:* Treat the apparent TOUSLESJOURS movement as a reporting-quality risk—not genuine demand growth—and exclude long-interval allocations from current demand reporting until the observation cadence is validated.", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "g6O1o", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*UTC analysis period:* previous window *2026-07-03 ~ 2026-07-09* versus current window *2026-07-10 ~ 2026-07-16*. *Base:* previous N=2,147,330 and current N=2,171,352 total inferred units.", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "hqISV", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Long-interval allocations represented "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2,166,889 of 2,171,352 inferred units (99.79%)", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " in the current window, up from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "75,794 of 2,147,330 (3.53%)", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " previously. Total inferred units increased by only "}, {"type": "text", "text": "24,022", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", while long-interval units increased by "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2,091,095", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", so the apparent movement is dominated by allocation methodology rather than a comparable demand signal. [1]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The long-interval share exceeded "}, {"type": "text", "text": "99.5% on every date from 2026-07-10 through 2026-07-16", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", after rising sharply between 2026-07-07 and 2026-07-09. [2]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The pattern is also present at the source-interval level: intervals longer than 24 hours rose to "}, {"type": "text", "text": "83,850 of 85,508 unique intervals (98.06%)", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "12,141 of 152,040 (7.99%)", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". [3]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is material beyond TOUSLESJOURS reporting: the affected "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2,166,889 units were 64.11% of 3,379,827 inferred units across all covered providers", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " in the current window. [4]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The increase was broad: the largest store contributed only "}, {"type": "text", "text": "11.49%", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " of the long-interval-unit increase. [5]"}]}], "style": "bullet", "indent": 0}]}, {"type": "image", "block_id": "RUi2v", "image_url": "https://velen.wordbricks.ai/api/assets/charts/xvRP1XDx1CzkG2E6d04KRZbFebcFhUi1/01KXQAQT3SCSDSPT2RHJC0PSE7/tlj_long_interval_share.png", "alt_text": "Daily share of TOUSLESJOURS inferred units allocated from long intervals", "image_width": 2084, "image_height": 1104, "image_bytes": 134146, "is_animated": true, "fallback": "2084x1104px image"}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "BrT8B", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "Observation gaps or crawler-cadence degradation are plausible hypotheses, but the operational cause is not proven. The current-state surface ends at *2026-07-14 21:58:41.734 UTC*, while the hourly surface extends to *2026-07-17 06:00:00 UTC*, reinforcing the need for run-level validation rather than a causal conclusion. [6] [7]", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "otyrO", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Recommended actions", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "f1uzg", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Demand-reporting owner:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " In TOUSLESJOURS dashboards and downstream demand extracts, immediately quarantine rows where "}, {"type": "text", "text": "interval_quality_status = ''long_interval''", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " or "}, {"type": "text", "text": "interval_duration_seconds > 86400", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": "; publish both included and excluded unit totals so stakeholders can verify the reporting impact. [1]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Crawler/data-engineering owner:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " Inspect run-level crawler logs and observation-completion metrics around "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2026-07-07 ~ 2026-07-09 UTC", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", segmented by store, to identify missed or delayed observation runs before deciding whether to reprocess affected intervals. [2] [5]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data-platform owner:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " Refresh "}, {"type": "text", "text": "current_store_item_state", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", then reconcile its latest TOUSLESJOURS observation timestamp against "}, {"type": "text", "text": "hourly_inferred_sales", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": "; restore current reporting only after the freshness gap and long-interval share return to an accepted threshold. [6] [7]"}]}], "style": "ordered", "indent": 0}]}]'),
