  ('ab24b95c-faba-5a30-b078-fe298a5ca917', '6c8eb00a-f68f-5306-9d35-ae99f729e52b', null, 'usr-slack-velen', 'CVS-9  :large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: curated_promotions_v2.promotion_snapshot_coverage  _Have feedback on this insight?_  Promotion snapshot continuity collapsed after 2026-07-07 UTC  *Decision:* Treat the promotion coverage break as an analytical observability/data-pipeline issue. Pause cross-provider promotion-performance analysis until coverage is restored or the expected-coverage denominator is documented.  *UTC comparison:* `2026-07-01 ~ 2026-07-07` versus `2026-07-08 ~ 2026-07-14`. *Fixed base:* N=118,454 eligible provider-store-days in each seven-day window, representing N=16,922 observed provider-store pairs. [1] [2]  Promotion snapshot continuity—observed provider-store-days divided by the fixed eligible base—fell from *15.9302% to 2.5470%*, a decline of *13.3833 percentage points* and *84.0117% relative*. Provider representation simultaneously fell from four providers to one. [1]  Promotion snapshot continuity across equal UTC windows  Scope and interpretation  - 16,491 of 16,922 provider-store pairs (97.4530%) were fully absent in the current window after appearing in the previous window. [2] - CU accounted for 15,808 net lost provider-store-days, or 99.7161% of the total net loss. [3] - Both windows contained one schema version and one transform version, even as represented providers fell from four to one. This does not support a version-count change as the explanation, but it does not establish another cause. [4] - The curated coverage surface ends on 2026-07-14, with one provider and 431 stores represented on that date; current server time is 2026-07-19 UTC. [5]  This is a measurement-coverage finding—not evidence that physical stores stopped running promotions. The available evidence identifies the break but does not establish its cause.  Recommended actions  1. Promotion data owners: Reconcile the expected promotion-producing providers and provider-store pairs against curated_promotions_v2.promotion_snapshot_coverage beginning after 2026-07-07 UTC. Document the expected providers, stores, service dates, and expected provider-store-day denominator needed to distinguish missing data from intentionally inactive coverage. 2. Ingestion and transformation owners: In the raw-arrival logs, parser logs, and materialization job records, compare object arrival counts, arrival timestamps, parse success/failure counts, and materialized row counts for CU, 7ELEVEN, GS25, and EMART24 beginning after 2026-07-07 UTC. Prioritize CU because it contributed 99.7161% of the observed net loss. [3] 3. Promotion analytics owners: Pause cross-provider promotion lift and performance reporting until provider-store coverage is restored or a documented expected-coverage denominator is implemented in the reporting layer.', '2026-07-19T08:00:13.553Z', '2026-07-19T08:00:13.553Z', '[{"type": "header", "block_id": "dZoak", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "CVS-9", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "context", "block_id": "dimUz", "elements": [{"type": "mrkdwn", "text": ":large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: curated_promotions_v2.promotion_snapshot_coverage", "verbatim": false}]}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "slack_feedback_open_block", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "_Have feedback on this insight?_", "verbatim": false}, "accessory": {"type": "button", "action_id": "slack_feedback_open", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Feedback", "emoji": true}, "accessibility_label": "Share feedback on this insight", "value": "{\"insightId\":\"01KXWEBAFTPW65VCN4DBJR8KVX\",\"source\":\"slack_message_button\"}"}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "n9HNI", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Promotion snapshot continuity collapsed after 2026-07-07 UTC", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "wQi5j", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*Decision:* Treat the promotion coverage break as an analytical observability/data-pipeline issue. Pause cross-provider promotion-performance analysis until coverage is restored or the expected-coverage denominator is documented.", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "NhQ7u", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*UTC comparison:* `2026-07-01 ~ 2026-07-07` versus `2026-07-08 ~ 2026-07-14`. *Fixed base:* N=118,454 eligible provider-store-days in each seven-day window, representing N=16,922 observed provider-store pairs. [1] [2]", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "41D6b", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "Promotion snapshot continuity—observed provider-store-days divided by the fixed eligible base—fell from *15.9302% to 2.5470%*, a decline of *13.3833 percentage points* and *84.0117% relative*. Provider representation simultaneously fell from four providers to one. [1]", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "image", "block_id": "oR4ze", "image_url": "https://velen.wordbricks.ai/api/assets/charts/xvRP1XDx1CzkG2E6d04KRZbFebcFhUi1/01KXWBXQZ7125X4SDG1AJMEM4N/promotion_snapshot_continuity.png", "alt_text": "Promotion snapshot continuity across equal UTC windows", "image_width": 1458, "image_height": 864, "image_bytes": 83049, "is_animated": true, "fallback": "1458x864px image"}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "6RIdx", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Scope and interpretation", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "L86Xj", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "16,491 of 16,922 provider-store pairs (97.4530%)", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " were fully absent in the current window after appearing in the previous window. [2]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "CU accounted for 15,808 net lost provider-store-days, or 99.7161% of the total net loss.", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " [3]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Both windows contained one schema version and one transform version, even as represented providers fell from four to one. This does "}, {"type": "text", "text": "not", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " support a version-count change as the explanation, but it does not establish another cause. [4]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The curated coverage surface ends on "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2026-07-14", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", with one provider and 431 stores represented on that date; current server time is "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2026-07-19 UTC", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". [5]"}]}], "style": "bullet", "indent": 0}]}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "m7mbB", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "This is a measurement-coverage finding—not evidence that physical stores stopped running promotions. The available evidence identifies the break but does not establish its cause.", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "1y7bw", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Recommended actions", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "5mjsA", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Promotion data owners:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " Reconcile the expected promotion-producing providers and provider-store pairs against "}, {"type": "text", "text": "curated_promotions_v2.promotion_snapshot_coverage", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " beginning after "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2026-07-07 UTC", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Document the expected providers, stores, service dates, and expected provider-store-day denominator needed to distinguish missing data from intentionally inactive coverage."}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ingestion and transformation owners:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " In the raw-arrival logs, parser logs, and materialization job records, compare object arrival counts, arrival timestamps, parse success/failure counts, and materialized row counts for "}, {"type": "text", "text": "CU, 7ELEVEN, GS25, and EMART24", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " beginning after "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2026-07-07 UTC", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Prioritize CU because it contributed "}, {"type": "text", "text": "99.7161%", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " of the observed net loss. [3]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Promotion analytics owners:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " Pause cross-provider promotion lift and performance reporting until provider-store coverage is restored or a documented expected-coverage denominator is implemented in the reporting layer."}]}], "style": "ordered", "indent": 0}]}]'),
  ('05b25384-b7f8-5e32-83bc-63e1d3ecba8c', 'ce5b2b18-914c-57af-aef4-fd0a71464e97', null, 'usr-slack-sophia', '<@U0BC2QD0GEN> 저는 지난번 프랜차이즈 박람회 가서, ‘카톡으로 주문받는 플로우’ 가 놀라운 포인트였는데,
크라이 치즈 버거에서도 단체주문은 전화로 받는다는게 이해가 되면서도 한번 더 생각해볼 수 있는 여지가 있는 부분이라고 느껴졌어요.

혹시 국내에 이렇게 카톡/문자/전화로 받아주는 솔루션 같은게 있는지, 있다면 어떤 형태인지 리서치 범위에 추가하는것에 대해 어떻게 생각하시나요?

우리가 발주 전 자동화를 한다면, 이렇게 전화를 대신 해주거나, 받아주는거에 대한 니즈도 있을지 탐색해볼 수 있을 것 같아요.', '2026-07-19T08:02:40.257Z', '2026-07-19T08:02:40.257Z', '[{"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "6ip5i", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "user", "user_id": "U0BC2QD0GEN"}, {"type": "text", "text": " 저는 지난번 프랜차이즈 박람회 가서, ‘카톡으로 주문받는 플로우’ 가 놀라운 포인트였는데,\n크라이 치즈 버거에서도 단체주문은 전화로 받는다는게 이해가 되면서도 한번 더 생각해볼 수 있는 여지가 있는 부분이라고 느껴졌어요.\n\n혹시 국내에 이렇게 카톡/문자/전화로 받아주는 솔루션 같은게 있는지, 있다면 어떤 형태인지 리서치 범위에 추가하는것에 대해 어떻게 생각하시나요?\n\n우리가 발주 전 자동화를 한다면, 이렇게 전화를 대신 해주거나, 받아주는거에 대한 니즈도 있을지 탐색해볼 수 있을 것 같아요."}]}]}]'),
  ('b3eb2d01-246f-5a0d-85cb-e5e9f5def023', 'ce5b2b18-914c-57af-aef4-fd0a71464e97', null, 'usr-slack-jayce', '아 네 알겠습니다 유효한 접근인 것 같고 
그부분도 대행해주는 업체가 있는지 확인해보도록하겠습니다', '2026-07-19T08:11:05.234Z', '2026-07-19T08:11:05.234Z', '[{"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "kEByN", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "아"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "네"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "알겠습니다"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "유효한"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "접근인"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "것"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "같고"}, {"type": "text", "text": " \n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "그부분도"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "대행해주는"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "업체가"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "있는지"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "확인해보도록하겠습니다"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}]}]}]'),
