  ('5ace9a08-4e7c-5910-8f35-dbf5afac050c', '6c8eb00a-f68f-5306-9d35-ae99f729e52b', null, 'usr-slack-velen', 'CVS-10  :large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: curated_inventory_v2.stock_events, curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales  _Have feedback on this insight?_  CU crawl coverage weakened, making inferred-sales movement unsafe for sales decisions  *Decision: actual sales judgment — insufficient evidence.* Treat the latest CU inferred-sales movement as an observation-coverage risk, *not an underlying sales decline*, until crawl completeness is controlled. The analysis uses UTC and compares *2026-07-13 ~ 2026-07-19* with *2026-07-06 ~ 2026-07-12*.  What changed  - The current-period base fell to N=860,406 stock-event rows, 6,897 distinct runs, and 2,706 observed store-days, from N=1,265,078 rows, 9,171 runs, and 2,724 store-days. That is a 31.99% drop in stock-event rows and a 24.80% drop in runs, while store-days changed only -0.66%. This pattern indicates materially thinner observation production within a nearly stable store-day footprint. [1] - Long-interval rows—allocations spanning unusually long observation gaps—increased from 11.61% to 18.78% of hourly rows, adding temporal-allocation risk. [2] - Coverage-normalized weighted inferred units moved in the opposite direction from the unadjusted result: 129.09 to 161.37 units per 1,000 stock-event rows, a 25.01% increase. Stock-event rows are only a coverage proxy because they do not record every attempted crawl. [3] - The uncertainty check is also inconclusive: N=7 same-weekday paired days produced a 95% interval of -36.06 to +15.40 units per active store, crossing zero. [4]  CU week-over-week observation coverage changes  Why this matters  The available data cannot separate a demand change from reduced or uneven crawl production. Using the unadjusted inferred-sales decline for category, store, or item decisions could therefore redirect action toward an instrumentation artifact rather than customer demand. [3] [4] [1]  Recommended actions  1. Data Engineering: obtain or build a crawl manifest at provider × store_cd × scheduled crawl grain. In the ingestion control layer, capture attempted/successful status, observed and expected item counts, completion timestamp, and failure reason so analysts have a complete crawl denominator. [5] [6] 2. Analytics: rerun the two UTC windows using only stores with successful, complete crawls in matched weekday/hour slots. Compare weighted inferred units per matched successful crawl and per matched observed store-item opportunity; proceed to category or store decomposition only if both coverage-controlled measures decline. [3] [4] 3. BI owners: label CU inferred-sales reporting for these dates as insufficient evidence for actual sales direction and pause sales interventions until the manifest-based matched comparison is available. [3] [1]', '2026-07-20T08:00:12.520Z', '2026-07-20T08:00:12.520Z', '[{"type": "header", "block_id": "fbvVt", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "CVS-10", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "context", "block_id": "y+NTF", "elements": [{"type": "mrkdwn", "text": ":large_orange_circle: High  •  cvs-analytics: curated_inventory_v2.stock_events, curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales", "verbatim": false}]}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "slack_feedback_open_block", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "_Have feedback on this insight?_", "verbatim": false}, "accessory": {"type": "button", "action_id": "slack_feedback_open", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Feedback", "emoji": true}, "accessibility_label": "Share feedback on this insight", "value": "{\"insightId\":\"01KXZ00F33CXY986DG494D2D63\",\"source\":\"slack_message_button\"}"}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "xV6Ik", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "CU crawl coverage weakened, making inferred-sales movement unsafe for sales decisions", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "wvUFC", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*Decision: actual sales judgment — insufficient evidence.* Treat the latest CU inferred-sales movement as an observation-coverage risk, *not an underlying sales decline*, until crawl completeness is controlled. The analysis uses UTC and compares *2026-07-13 ~ 2026-07-19* with *2026-07-06 ~ 2026-07-12*.", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "PGI+q", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "What changed", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "WwFgI", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The current-period base fell to "}, {"type": "text", "text": "N=860,406 stock-event rows", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "text", "text": "6,897 distinct runs", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2,706 observed store-days", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "N=1,265,078 rows", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "text", "text": "9,171 runs", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and "}, {"type": "text", "text": "2,724 store-days", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". That is a "}, {"type": "text", "text": "31.99% drop in stock-event rows", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " and a "}, {"type": "text", "text": "24.80% drop in runs", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", while store-days changed only "}, {"type": "text", "text": "-0.66%", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". This pattern indicates materially thinner observation production within a nearly stable store-day footprint. [1]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Long-interval rows—allocations spanning unusually long observation gaps—increased from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "11.61% to 18.78%", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " of hourly rows, adding temporal-allocation risk. [2]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Coverage-normalized weighted inferred units moved in the opposite direction from the unadjusted result: "}, {"type": "text", "text": "129.09 to 161.37 units per 1,000 stock-event rows", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", a "}, {"type": "text", "text": "25.01% increase", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Stock-event rows are only a coverage proxy because they do not record every attempted crawl. [3]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The uncertainty check is also inconclusive: "}, {"type": "text", "text": "N=7 same-weekday paired days", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " produced a 95% interval of "}, {"type": "text", "text": "-36.06 to +15.40 units per active store", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", crossing zero. [4]"}]}], "style": "bullet", "indent": 0}]}, {"type": "image", "block_id": "eV9QN", "image_url": "https://velen.wordbricks.ai/api/assets/charts/xvRP1XDx1CzkG2E6d04KRZbFebcFhUi1/01KXYYAF6251R2R06XKQFMPDDR/cu_coverage_deterioration.png", "alt_text": "CU week-over-week observation coverage changes", "image_width": 2103, "image_height": 1162, "image_bytes": 114662, "is_animated": true, "fallback": "2103x1162px image"}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "lcJed", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Why this matters", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "5+oG1", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "The available data cannot separate a demand change from reduced or uneven crawl production. Using the unadjusted inferred-sales decline for category, store, or item decisions could therefore redirect action toward an instrumentation artifact rather than customer demand. [3] [4] [1]", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "pTiFc", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Recommended actions", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "2dDfg", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data Engineering:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " obtain or build a crawl manifest at "}, {"type": "text", "text": "provider × store_cd × scheduled crawl", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " grain. In the ingestion control layer, capture attempted/successful status, observed and expected item counts, completion timestamp, and failure reason so analysts have a complete crawl denominator. [5] [6]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Analytics:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " rerun the two UTC windows using only stores with successful, complete crawls in matched weekday/hour slots. Compare weighted inferred units per matched successful crawl and per matched observed store-item opportunity; proceed to category or store decomposition only if both coverage-controlled measures decline. [3] [4]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "BI owners:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " label CU inferred-sales reporting for these dates as "}, {"type": "text", "text": "insufficient evidence for actual sales direction", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " and pause sales interventions until the manifest-based matched comparison is available. [3] [1]"}]}], "style": "ordered", "indent": 0}]}]'),
