insert into briar_channel_messages (id, channel_id, parent_message_id, author_user_id, body, created_at, updated_at, blocks_json)
values
  ('6daa10bd-3221-52fa-865c-1c1852f14aa1', '6c8eb00a-f68f-5306-9d35-ae99f729e52b', '58ced7cd-f4ac-56e0-8e00-24e667d3eeb7', 'usr-slack-velen', 'For the last 30 days in UTC (MAY 13, 2026 04:36:51 → JUN 12, 2026 04:36:51), I found *no CU stock snapshot rows*, so there is *no per-day CU stock total to report*. The daily CU stock query returned *0 rows* from `inventory_snapshots` and *0 rows* from `store_inventory_snapshots`. [QID: 1] [QID: 2]  I also checked overall table coverage: `inventory_snapshots` is empty, and `store_inventory_snapshots` has data in the period only for `OLIVEYOUNG`, not `CU`. [QID: 3] [QID: 4]  Knowledge graph lookup could not be used because the org Cognee configuration is missing (`baseUrl` / `apiKey`), so I relied on the connected database only.  Analysis Period  - Timezone: UTC - Period: MAY 13, 2026 04:36:51 through JUN 12, 2026 04:36:51 - CU daily stock rows found: 0 - N: 0 CU snapshot rows  Exact SQL Used  SELECT date(checked_at) AS day,        COUNT(*) AS snapshot_rows,        COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS stores,        COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS products,        SUM(COALESCE(quantity,0)) AS total_stock FROM inventory_snapshots WHERE brand = ''CU''   AND checked_at &gt;= datetime(''now'',''-30 days'')   AND checked_at &lt; datetime(''now'') GROUP BY date(checked_at) ORDER BY day;  SELECT date(checked_at) AS day,        COUNT(*) AS snapshot_rows,        COUNT(DISTINCT store_cd) AS stores,        COUNT(DISTINCT item_cd) AS items,        SUM(COALESCE(stock,0)) AS total_stock FROM store_inventory_snapshots WHERE brand = ''CU''   AND checked_at &gt;= datetime(''now'',''-30 days'')   AND checked_at &lt; datetime(''now'') GROUP BY date(checked_at) ORDER BY day;  Analysis Worklog  1. Identified available inventory-related tables in the connected D1 database.  SELECT name, type FROM sqlite_master WHERE type IN (''table'',''view'') ORDER BY name LIMIT 200;  Learned that relevant tables include `inventory_snapshots`, `inventory_latest_state`, `store_inventory_snapshots`, and related inventory/store tables. [QID: 5]  1. Inspected the table definitions to identify stock and timestamp fields.  SELECT sql FROM sqlite_master WHERE name IN (''inventory_snapshots'',''inventory_latest_state'',''products'',''store_inventory_snapshots'') ORDER BY name;  Learned that `inventory_snapshots` uses `quantity`, `store_id`, `product_id`, and `checked_at`, while `store_inventory_snapshots` uses `stock`, `store_cd`, `item_cd`, and `checked_at`. [QID: 6]  1. Queried CU daily stock totals for the last 30 days from both candidate snapshot tables.  SELECT date(checked_at) AS day,        COUNT(*) AS snapshot_rows,        COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS stores,        COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS products,        SUM(COALESCE(quantity,0)) AS total_stock FROM inventory_snapshots WHERE brand = ''CU''   AND checked_at &gt;= datetime(''now'',''-30 days'')   AND checked_at &lt; datetime(''now'') GROUP BY date(checked_at) ORDER BY day;  Learned that `inventory_snapshots` returned 0 CU daily rows for the period. [QID: 1]  SELECT MIN(checked_at) AS min_checked_at,        MAX(checked_at) AS max_checked_at,        COUNT(*) AS rows_in_period FROM inventory_snapshots WHERE brand = ''CU''   AND checked_at &gt;= datetime(''now'',''-30 days'')   AND checked_at &lt; datetime(''now'');  Learned that `inventory_snapshots` has 0 CU rows in the period. [QID: 7]  SELECT MIN(checked_at) AS min_checked_at,        MAX(checked_at) AS max_checked_at,        COUNT(*) AS total_rows,        COUNT(DISTINCT brand) AS brands FROM inventory_snapshots;  Learned that `inventory_snapshots` is empty overall. [QID: 3]  SELECT brand,        COUNT(*) AS rows,        MIN(checked_at) AS min_checked_at,        MAX(checked_at) AS max_checked_at FROM inventory_snapshots GROUP BY brand ORDER BY rows DESC LIMIT 20;  Learned that there are no brand-level rows in `inventory_snapshots`. [QID: 8]  SELECT MIN(checked_at) AS min_checked_at,        MAX(checked_at) AS max_checked_at,        COUNT(*) AS total_rows,        COUNT(DISTINCT brand) AS brands FROM store_inventory_snapshots;  Learned that `store_inventory_snapshots` contains 5,007 rows overall, with timestamps on MAY 27, 2026 UTC. [QID: 9', '2026-06-12T04:39:03.602Z', '2026-06-12T04:39:03.602Z', '[{"type": "section", "block_id": "610/c", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "For the last 30 days in UTC (MAY 13, 2026 04:36:51 → JUN 12, 2026 04:36:51), I found *no CU stock snapshot rows*, so there is *no per-day CU stock total to report*. The daily CU stock query returned *0 rows* from `inventory_snapshots` and *0 rows* from `store_inventory_snapshots`. [QID: 1] [QID: 2]", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "wCeqM", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "I also checked overall table coverage: `inventory_snapshots` is empty, and `store_inventory_snapshots` has data in the period only for `OLIVEYOUNG`, not `CU`. [QID: 3] [QID: 4]", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "g6UeV", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "Knowledge graph lookup could not be used because the org Cognee configuration is missing (`baseUrl` / `apiKey`), so I relied on the connected database only.", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "5Z+Rj", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Analysis Period", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "YbBqZ", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Timezone:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " UTC"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Period:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " MAY 13, 2026 04"}, {"type": "emoji", "name": "36"}, {"type": "text", "text": "51 through JUN 12, 2026 04"}, {"type": "emoji", "name": "36"}, {"type": "text", "text": "51"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "CU daily stock rows found:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " 0"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "N:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " 0 CU snapshot rows"}]}], "style": "bullet", "indent": 0}]}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "SwWJU", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Exact SQL Used", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "C7LQa", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_preformatted", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "SELECT date(checked_at) AS day,\n       COUNT(*) AS snapshot_rows,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS stores,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS products,\n       SUM(COALESCE(quantity,0)) AS total_stock\nFROM inventory_snapshots\nWHERE brand = ''CU''\n  AND checked_at >= datetime(''now'',''-30 days'')\n  AND checked_at < datetime(''now'')\nGROUP BY date(checked_at)\nORDER BY day;"}]}]}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "YZKg9", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_preformatted", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "SELECT date(checked_at) AS day,\n       COUNT(*) AS snapshot_rows,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT store_cd) AS stores,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT item_cd) AS items,\n       SUM(COALESCE(stock,0)) AS total_stock\nFROM store_inventory_snapshots\nWHERE brand = ''CU''\n  AND checked_at >= datetime(''now'',''-30 days'')\n  AND checked_at < datetime(''now'')\nGROUP BY date(checked_at)\nORDER BY day;"}]}]}, {"type": "header", "block_id": "35ydO", "text": {"type": "plain_text", "text": "Analysis Worklog", "emoji": true}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "bIp5/", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Identified available inventory-related tables in the connected D1 database."}]}], "style": "ordered", "indent": 0}]}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "lLo6t", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_preformatted", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "SELECT name, type\nFROM sqlite_master\nWHERE type IN (''table'',''view'')\nORDER BY name\nLIMIT 20