  ('16e9d02c-3c94-5dcc-8be6-a3c2d5ee71a4', '6c8eb00a-f68f-5306-9d35-ae99f729e52b', '51e0b0ee-0fc7-57a3-8651-d626db3ce581', 'usr-slack-velen', '- Data engineering: audit the curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales transform and backfill coverage for TOUSLESJOURS, specifically the jump in active stores from 216 previous-window stores to 1,023 current-window stores, and identify whether coverage, allocation logic, or upstream availability changed. [5] - Analytics / BI owners: temporarily flag or exclude TOUSLESJOURS inferred sales from executive reporting, forecasting inputs, and promotion readouts until the coverage/backfill explanation is documented, because it accounts for 56.03961871736214% of current inferred units. [3] - Commercial / category team: avoid treating the spike as demand growth until engineering reconciles hourly_inferred_sales against stock_events; the raw stock-event footprint does not support the same scale of expansion. [5]', '2026-07-08T08:00:15.627Z', '2026-07-08T08:00:15.627Z', '[{"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "sDrgf", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data engineering:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " audit the "}, {"type": "text", "text": "curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " transform and backfill coverage for "}, {"type": "text", "text": "TOUSLESJOURS", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", specifically the jump in active stores from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "216", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " previous-window stores to "}, {"type": "text", "text": "1,023", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " current-window stores, and identify whether coverage, allocation logic, or upstream availability changed. [5]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Analytics / BI owners:", "style": {