ed from transform "}, {"type": "text", "text": "inventory-events-jsonl-to-hourly-inferred-sales-v1.0.0", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " / schema "}, {"type": "text", "text": "v1", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " to transform "}, {"type": "text", "text": "inventory-events-jsonl-to-hourly-inferred-sales-v2.0.0", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " / schema "}, {"type": "text", "text": "v2", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": "; the latest week uses the latter version. [6]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "The interval-quality population simultaneously shifted from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "NULL", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " toward "}, {"type": "text", "text": "long_interval", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", with large opposing contributions to estimated-sales amount. This is a definition/logging-change signal, not proof of cause. [7] [8]"}]}], "style": "bullet", "indent": 0}]}, {"type": "section", "block_id": "jPSZw", "text": {"type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*Recommended actions*", "verbatim": false}}, {"type": "rich_text", "block_id": "fJ/nt", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_list", "elements": [{"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data Engineering:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " Reprocess both UTC windows in "}, {"type": "text", "text": "curated_inventory_v2.hourly_inferred_sales", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " under one transform/schema version. Record resulting fact rows, active item-store pairs, inferred units, and estimated-sales amount for each window so comparability can be confirmed."}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data Quality:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " Audit source intervals and allocation behavior for stores "}, {"type": "text", "text": "1112150", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "text", "text": "1112179", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "text", "text": "1101323", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "text", "text": "1111389", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and "}, {"type": "text", "text": "1110280", "style": {"code": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": ", focusing on the preceding-week to latest-week transition and identifying whether their near-total measured decline reflects missing coverage, interval handling, or valid source activity. [4] [5]"}]}, {"type": "rich_text_section", "elements": [{"type": "text", "text": "Analytics:", "style": {"bold": true}}, {"type": "text", "text": " After reprocessing, rerun the provider and store decompositions and withhold commercial interpretation until the coverage, quality-status, and weekly totals reconcile on the common version."}]}], "style": "ordered", "indent": 0}]}]')
